  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Offshore Pre Migration Health Activities to New Zealand Refugee Quota Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is intended to provide resettlement (medical) assistance to New Zealand Refugee Quota Programme (RQP) and RQP applicants, in accordance with their roadmap to accommodate its annual refugee quota recently doubled to 1500. In the MOU and Framework Agreement between IOM and the Ministry of Business, Innovation and Employment (MBIE), in this particular project, IOM will provide Immigration New Zealand (INZ), under the umbrella of MBIE, with pre-migration health assistance, including immigration medical exam (IME), settlement health assessment (SHA) and departure health check (DHC) to establish fitness to travel and provide resettlement travel assistance from their country of refuge to New Zealand.</narrative>
  </description>
